    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29340" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mnēmŏsynē</span></b> ,
			ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μνημοσύνη</span> (remembrance). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The mother of the Muses</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 6,
				114</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D. 3, 31, 54</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Phaedr. 3</span></i>
			prol. 18: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">natae Mnemosynes,</span>”
				<i>the Muses</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Ep. 4, 64</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
				plur.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mnēmŏ-synae</span></b> ,
				ārum, f., <i>the Muses</i>, <i><span class="en">Aus. Idyll. 11,
			30</span></i>.</div>
